# 00 — THE MISSION

I want you to make WORLD SIGNAL genuinely beautiful, distinctive, attractive, and enjoyable to use.

Not merely clean.

Not merely functional.

Not merely technically sophisticated.

The current product has substantial functionality and a growing editorial design system, but it still needs a more compelling visual identity and a more sophisticated reader experience.

The next phase must transform the frontend into a premium contemporary global affairs publication.

The visual experience should combine:

1. The authority of an international newspaper.
2. The art direction of a premium editorial magazine.
3. The visual storytelling of a top-tier journalism publication.
4. The information clarity of a professional intelligence research platform.
5. The usability of a polished modern digital product.

**I want the result to look authored, composed, and art-directed — not generated from a generic UI template.**

The most important goal:

Make a visitor want to stay, explore stories, read deeper, and return.

Visual quality is a central product requirement.

