## 6.4 Evidence indicators

The hero currently includes several numerical indicators.

Assess whether all of them deserve the same visual prominence.

Keep the useful evidence facts:

- Independent reporting origins.
- Claim counts and statuses.
- Source count.
- Real timeline span.

However, do not make the cover resemble an analytical KPI dashboard.

Separate the visual story from detailed verification statistics when this improves comprehension.

Do not remove the underlying evidence information.

Make it accessible in an appropriate secondary presentation.

## 6.5 Executive Summary

Improve the summary into a compelling editorial briefing section.

Do not display a large paragraph as a dense block.

Use:

- A clear introductory hierarchy.
- Comfortable reading measure.
- Good paragraph spacing.
- Appropriate emphasis from the actual Markdown content.
- Elegant expand/collapse behavior.
- A clearer relationship with the edition's domain coverage and caveats.

Keep the complete underlying summary.

Do not invent bullets or rewrite editorial facts merely to fit the design.

## 6.6 Secondary stories

The current secondary hierarchy is a useful foundation.

Preserve its functional editorial ranking:

- Lead feature.
- Secondary feature.
- Supporting pair.
- Compact dispatch index.

Improve the visual quality of each story level.

Avoid making every item a uniform image card.

A strong publication uses different visual weights for different editorial roles.

## 6.7 Three Domain Desks

The current three-column domain section should evolve beyond three similar columns with domain images.

Create distinctive editorial desk identities.

World Events, AI Frontier, and Economic Outlook should feel like three recognizable desks within one publication.

Explore:

- Different editorial layouts.
- Unique accent treatment.
- Domain-specific story groupings.
- Actual domain coverage information.
- Featured stories with compelling headlines.
- Compact lower-priority story indexes.

Do not invent domain metrics.

Do not simply duplicate the same visual structure three times.

## 6.8 Daily Delta and Catch-Up

Keep all existing functions.

Make these sections feel like professional newsroom products:

- Daily Delta should communicate material developments.
- Catch-Up should provide a quick and useful reading checkpoint.
- Arbitrary comparison should remain accessible.

